ain analysis fields.","id":"declaration:LongTails.Setups.MuonSpectral.publicInput","source":["src_969f18856b5c57ac143274ca","src_1d84230d8e108553e6f125eb","src_c96c76cc243c6c38026c34db","src_b721ba6a9e723e37ed12c430","src_eb7917a5f6ea922d685bf64a","src_0e774d5ee74c495be3ccdf27","src_31a9112775ab7471dca09b29","src_5b5798caa9f750cef56b0be2"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/declaration_evidence/LongTails.Setups.MuonSpectral.spec/preferred"],"comparison":"The exact Setup uses hidden objective f as Instance, real matrices as Query/Reply and Fin(T+1) trajectories as Output. Validity imposes positive dimensions, eta and T>=1, plus nonnegative smoothness/sigma, 0<=beta<1 and B>=1. Admissibility is the original analytic assumption, BddBelow(range f), and the shared stochastic oracle model. Successful is the original internal Guarantee under the given probability law and allowedAlgorithm is exactly the source method.","id":"declaration:LongTails.Setups.MuonSpectral.spec","source":["src_969f18856b5c57ac143274ca","src_1d84230d8e108553e6f125eb","src_c96c76cc243c6c38026c34db","src_b721ba6a9e723e37ed12c430","src_eb7917a5f6ea922d685bf64a","src_0e774d5ee74c495be3ccdf27","src_31a9112775ab7471dca09b29","src_5b5798caa9f750cef56b0be2"],"verdict":"match"},{"candidate":["candidate/declaration_evidence/LongTails.Setups.MuonSpectral.SpectralSmooth/preferred","candidate/declaration_evidence/LongTails.Setups.MuonSpectral.spec/preferred"],"comparison":"The predicate requires HasGradientAt at every point and nuclearNorm(grad f W-grad f Wprime) <= Ls*spectralNorm(W-Wprime). This is Assumption 3.2; neither side is replaced by a Frobenius norm.","id":"node:A32","source":["src_969f18856b5c57ac143274ca","src_1d84230d8e108553e6f125eb","src_c96c76cc243c6c38026c34db","src_b721ba6a9e723e37ed12c430","src_eb7917a5f6ea922d685bf64a","src_0e774d5ee74c495be3ccdf27","src_31a9112775ab7471dca09b29","src_5b5798caa9f750cef56b0be2"],"verdict":"match"}],"notes":["This accepts an unchanged internal source